es it to 4 using its actual old last-log tuple. B term-4 request has the fresh tuple; the failed candidate-key write leaves old A with successfully stored term 4. The driver substitutes timer/main-loop scheduling and later B candidacy; that transition can occur after quorum loss and election timeout and neither changes V vote memory nor supplies the tested grant. Individual successful stable writes remain intact, and the failed Set returns an ordinary error without corruption. The driver does not fake a prior same-term grant: history of actual V responses is inspected at final admission.','applicability':'Local RequestVote freshness after a partial vote persistence error, plus same-sequence successful-write control. Fixed IDs/addresses, no concurrent node mutation during each phase.','unresolved':[],'conflicts':[],'alternatives':['The driver does not execute lease/election timers or an eventual stale-leader election; those are outside the local grant responsibility.','Storage backends that stop the process instead of returning the injected error do not exercise this conditional continuation.']}},'monitors':[{'id':'monitor-vote-freshness','checker_id':'vote-freshness','event':'vote_result','binding_ids':bind,'admission_alias':'admitted','applicability_conditions':[],'grounding':{'source_ids':ss,'binding_ids':bind,'derivation':'Admission independently computes log staleness from actual request and receiver log tuples and checks actual prior V response history for same candidate/term grant. Compare the subsequent actual Granted response with false. Distinct operation names correlate each control/discriminator prefix, admission and completed reply. The result is emitted even when granted, not filtered by expected outcome.','applicability':'A log-stale request without previous same-term grant; fault branch has the documented partial pair and successful control has the other candidate saved.','unresolved':[],'conflicts':[]}}],'observable_properties':[{'checker_id':'vote-freshness','kind':'event_assertion','trigger':{'field':'event','value':'vote_result'},'assertion':{'field':'granted','value':False},'identity_fields':['operation'],'description':'The stale candidate without a previous same-term grant must be denied; a new term paired with an old candidate after Set failure cannot serve as an eligibility exception.'}],'uncertainties':['No particular production storage backend is exercised; the error-return model is explicit.','Actual election RPC producers and log replication execute, but timer scheduling and leader transitions are driver-controlled.','No final stale-leader election or loss of a committed command is observed.']}\nopen('vote-plan.json','w').write(json.dumps(p,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nsub={'action':'check','unit_id':'unit-claim-vote-freshness-after-write-error','rationale':'Compare real stale RequestVote handling after successful versus failed candidate persistence, retaining generated request history, stored key observations and explicit scheduling substitutions.','plan_path':'vote-plan.json','harness_path':'vote_pair_test.go'}\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_13-58-41-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"07f36b754674425985b5610b78bed716\", \"audit_spec_version\": 3, \"elapsed_seconds\": 1576.232177789003, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Validation against the state and bytes read; this is not acceptance, execution or evidence\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
